# Laura Thomas Counselling

## Hard rules

- Single Composer session only — no subagents or parallel agents.
- Short placeholder copy until told otherwise; no long-form or SEO content.
- Never invent fees, credentials, contact details, or reviews; use clear placeholders.
- Never commit secrets; do not deploy or change DNS.
- Keep `docs/reference/` out of `public/` and the production bundle.
- No WordPress or legacy content migration (fetch, scrape, import, recreate, or inventory) unless Joshua explicitly approves — defer to a dedicated migration batch.
- **RULE A — NOT INDEXABLE:** Until Joshua approves launch, the whole build stays non-indexable (`SITE_INDEXABLE` defaults false): layout robots noindex/nofollow, global `X-Robots-Tag`, `robots.ts` `Disallow: /`, empty sitemap, no live-domain canonicals.
- **RULE B — PROTECT URLS:** Preserve every legacy path (trailing slashes) via `src/lib/routes.ts`; `trailingSlash: true`; no catch-alls or homepage redirects; articles registry-only until migration; `npm run check:routes` must pass.

## Workflow

- One batch per session per `COMPOSER_BATCHES.md`; Batch 0 is complete (infrastructure only); Batch 1 adds fonts, assets, header/footer.
- Do not build full Laura pages in Batch 0 scope; follow the next batch title exactly.
- Finish with green `npm run build` and `npm run lint`, then commit and stop.

## Assessment (Batch 0)

Next.js 16 App Router base repurposed from trusted-founders-club tooling (not a second scaffold). Product auth, payments, DB, and Review Signal UI were stripped. Laura forest/cream tokens are in `app/globals.css`. Local Cormorant + Inter fonts and Header/Footer shell are Batch 1. See `docs/CODEBASE_ASSESSMENT.md`.
